# asphodelos — how this repository is run

Generates type-safe [Elysia](https://elysiajs.com/) code — routes, TypeBox schemas, Eden
wrappers, client hooks, tests and a mock server — from OpenAPI or TypeSpec. Published to npm as
`asphodelos`, with a CLI and a Vite plugin. Built on Effect v4, formatted by oxfmt, linted by
oxlint, run and tested with Bun. It is the Elysia sibling of `nakita628/hono-takibi`; features
are often ported from there, adapted to what differs here.

This repository is operated **through agent conversation alone**. Nothing here assumes a human
will fix it up afterwards. The config files are the source of truth: when an instruction
contradicts one, quote the config and ask before changing it.

Everything committed is written in **English** — code, comments, TSDoc, Markdown, commit
messages, workflow comments. textlint and cspell assume it. Test data may be in any language.

## Layout

```text
packages/asphodelos/          the published package (the only npm artifact)
  src/                        implementation; see the architecture rule for the layering
  lint/custom.js              oxlint JS plugin holding this repo's structural conventions
  oxlint.config.ts            source of truth for lint (the comments are the design)
  tsdown.config.ts            build: one entry per `exports` subpath
test/                         client suite: compiles and runs the generated hooks, and the
                              packaged CLI and Vite plugin from dist
  cases/<name>/               one asphodelos.config.ts + tsconfig.json per client library
  oxlint.config.ts            reuses the package's rules; do not copy rules into it
scripts/actionlint.ts         downloads a pinned actionlint, verifies its checksum, runs it
scripts/pack-smoke.ts         installs the packed tarball with npm into an empty project and uses it
scripts/typespec.ts           fails when the @typespec/* packages in bun.lock are not one TypeSpec release
scripts/zizmor.ts             downloads a pinned zizmor (workflow security audit), verifies it, runs it
oxfmt.config.ts               source of truth for formatting (printWidth 100, single quotes, no semicolons)
renovate.json                 dependency updates (Saturdays, Asia/Tokyo); see the CI rule's Dependencies
.github/workflows/test.yaml   CI (Test): the same commands as below, in the same order
.github/workflows/release.yaml  after Test on main: tag, npm publish, GitHub release
```

## Commands

Run these from the repository root.

| Goal | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Install dependencies | `bun install --frozen-lockfile` |
| Everything CI checks, in CI's order | `bun run check` |
| Autofix formatting, oxlint, markdownlint and textlint | `bun run fix` |
| Linters (oxlint on the package, markdownlint, textlint, cspell, secretlint, the TypeSpec release check, actionlint, zizmor) | `bun run lint` |
| Type check the package | `bun run typecheck` |
| Unit tests | `bun run test` |
| Build `dist` | `bun run build` |
| Client suite: build, generate, typecheck, lint and run `test/` | `bun run test:clients` |
| npm tarball smoke test (builds first, needs network) | `bun run test:pack` |
| One test file | `bun -F asphodelos test src/<path>.test.ts` |

- `test:clients` runs the packaged CLI and Vite plugin from `dist`, so it always builds first.
  Never run `cd test && bun test` against a stale build.
- The `test/` workspace is linted inside `test:clients`, not `lint`: its type-aware rules read
  `test/__generated__`, which is gitignored and exists only after the generation step. A lint
  that ran before it would pass on a working copy that still has old output and fail on a fresh
  checkout.
- oxlint loads its TypeScript config through Node, which needs a Node that runs `.ts` natively
  (CI uses Node 24).

## Definition of done

Before reporting a task finished, **`bun run check` must be green**. One failure means not done.
If you only ran part of it, say which part.

- A behavior change ships with a test that fails before it and passes after.
- A change to the config, the CLI, the Vite plugin or the generated output updates
  `packages/asphodelos/README.md` in the same change (the user documentation and the config
  reference; the root `README.md` is a symlink to it).
- Report results as they are. Never call a task complete while hiding a failing command, and
  never make a check pass by weakening it.

## Invariants

- **Never relax a linter to get a change through.** Do not set a rule to `'off'`, do not lower
  `categories`, do not drop `denyWarnings`, do not add an `ignorePaths` / `ignorePatterns`
  entry to hide a finding. If a rule genuinely does not fit, say so and ask.
- **Suppressions live next to the code, naming the rule and the reason:**
  `// oxlint-disable-next-line rule-name -- reason`. Never disable a whole file.
  `reportUnusedDisableDirectives: 'deny'` is on, so a suppression that stopped firing must go.
- **No `TODO` / `FIXME`.** `no-warning-comments` rejects them in source, textlint's `no-todo`
  in docs. Parked work belongs in the report.
- **Failures are typed Effect errors, never throws**: `GenerateError`, `FormatError`,
  `OpenAPIError`, `ConfigError`, `PlatformError`. See the Effect rule.
- **Never hand-edit generated files:** `bun.lock` (let `bun install` write it), `dist/`,
  `test/__generated__/`, `tmp-*` work trees.
- **`elysia` and `test` output holds the user's code.** Those generators merge into what is on
  disk (`src/merge`). Nothing may delete or blindly overwrite that output.
- **`effect`, `@effect/platform-node` and `@effect/platform-node-shared` are pinned exactly**
  (`4.0.0-rc.112`, an rc whose API still moves) and move together, in one change. Leaving one of
  them to a range lets npm install a second `effect` for users, and the CLI then fails with
  "Service not found"; `bun run test:pack` checks that exactly one `effect` is installed.
- **Never bump `version` in `packages/asphodelos/package.json`** unless the task is a release
  that was asked for: pushing a new version to `main` is what publishes it. Never `npm publish`,
  `bun publish` or push a `v*` tag by hand — `.github/workflows/release.yaml` tags, publishes and
  releases, from one commit.

## Working order

1. Read the rules in force for the files you are about to touch (`rules` and `overrides` in
   `packages/asphodelos/oxlint.config.ts`, and the matching `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`).
2. Implement it the way the surrounding code is written. Do not introduce a second idiom.
3. `bun run fix`, then `bun run check`.
4. Commit and push (see Git policy).
5. In the final report state what changed, which commands verified it, and anything left out.

## Git policy

- The owner has authorized committing **directly to `main`** and pushing once `bun run check` is
  green. Never force-push and never rewrite pushed history.
- One logical change per commit. The subject is an imperative sentence in the shape of the
  existing history (`Generate the client cases before typechecking them`), with no `feat:` /
  `fix:` prefix; the body explains why. A version bump is its own commit, subject the version.
- Do not commit generated output, secrets or local tooling files.
